        "original_id": "93047ba5-7f17-5ffc-942c-86a1d7ffaab5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jocelyn Bell Burnell, Antony Hewish, Martin Ryle, John Arbuthnott, Lord Wilson of Tillyorn\n- Organizations: Royal Astronomical Society, Royal Society of Edinburgh\n- Roles: astrophysicist, postgraduate student, thesis supervisor, President of the Royal Society of Edinburgh\n- Discoveries and Awards: first radio pulsars, Nobel Prize in Physics, Eddington Medal\n\nFacts:\n- In 1969, Antony Hewish was awarded the Eddington Medal of the Royal Astronomical Society.\n- Dame Susan Jocelyn Bell Burnell was born on 15 July 1943 and is a Northern Irish astrophysicist.\n- As a postgraduate student, Jocelyn Bell Burnell discovered the first radio pulsars while studying under her thesis supervisor Antony Hewish.\n- Antony Hewish shared the Nobel Prize in Physics with astronomer Martin Ryle for work connected to the discovery of the first radio pulsars.\n- In October 2011, John Arbuthnott succeeded Lord Wilson of Tillyorn as President of the Royal Society of Edinburgh.\n- In October 2014, Dame Jocelyn Bell Burnell succeeded John Arbuthnott as President of the Royal Society of Edinburgh.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c7ac6cbc-940c-5993-8d7d-92cf4a32fa65",
        "text": "Page: Jocelyn Bell Burnell. Sentence: Dame Susan Jocelyn Bell Burnell, (born 15 July 1943) is a Northern Irish astrophysicist.\nPage: Jocelyn Bell Burnell. Sentence: As a postgraduate student, she discovered the first radio pulsars while studying and advised by her thesis supervisor Antony Hewish, for which Hewish shared the Nobel Prize in Physics with astronomer Martin Ryle.\nPage: Antony Hewish. Sentence: He was also awarded the Eddington Medal of the Royal Astronomical Society in 1969.\nPage: John Arbuthnott (microbiologist). Sentence: He succeeded Lord Wilson of Tillyorn as President of The Royal Society of Edinburgh in October 2011 and was succeeded by Dame Jocelyn Bell Burnell in October 2014.",
